<title>UK: NWE oil products mostly weaker with futures.</title>
<headline>NWE oil products mostly weaker with futures.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-01-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>NWE oil products were mostly weaker with futures on Friday, traders said.</p>
<p>Gasoline was $2-3 a tonne easier in line with weaker U.S gasoline. Naphtha also slipped $1-2 or so amid poor end-user buying.</p>
<p>Gas oil shed $4 on easier futures. Good heating oil demand lifted NWE premiums by $1 a tonne. Barge premiums were steady.</p>
<p>High sulphur cracked fuel oil shed $4 or $5, while low sulphur was steady or $1 firmer.</p>
<p>-- London newsroom +44 171 542 8167</p>
